## Integration Tests

### When to Use
- Repository adapters (real DB)
- External service adapters (real sandbox)

### Database Setup with mongodb-memory-server

```java
@Testcontainers
class TheOrderRepositoryIntegrationTest {

    @Container
    static PostgreSQLContainer<?> postgres = new PostgreSQLContainer<>("postgres:15");

    private OrderRepository repository;

    @BeforeEach
    void setup() {
        repository = new PostgresOrderRepository(postgres.getJdbcUrl());
        repository.clear();
    }

    @Test
    void persistsAndRetrievesOrder() {
        Order order = Order.create(Id.generate());

        repository.save(order);
        Order retrieved = repository.findById(order.getId()).orElse(null);

        assertEquals(order.getId(), retrieved.getId());
    }
}
```

### Rules
- **Real dependencies**: Use mongodb-memory-server for MongoDB
- **Isolation**: Each test cleans its own data (beforeEach)
- **No shared state**: Tests must not depend on order of execution
- **File naming**: `*IntegrationTest.java`

---

## E2E Tests

### When to Use
- Full HTTP flows through the API
- Critical user journeys

### Structure

```java
@SpringBootTest(webEnvironment = SpringBootTest.WebEnvironment.RANDOM_PORT)
class OrderCreationE2ETest {

    @Autowired
    private TestRestTemplate restTemplate;

    @BeforeEach
    void setup() {
        resetDatabase();
        seedProducts();
    }

    @Test
    void createsOrderAndConfirmsAvailability() {
        OrderRequest request = new OrderRequest(testProductId, 2);

        ResponseEntity<OrderResponse> response =
                restTemplate.postForEntity("/orders", request, OrderResponse.class);

        assertEquals(201, response.getStatusCodeValue());
        assertNotNull(response.getBody().getId());
    }
}
```

### Rules
- **Test flows, not endpoints**: Cover complete business scenarios
- **Factories/fixtures**: Use factories to create test data
- **Clean slate**: Reset database before each test
- **Sandbox for externals**: External services use test/sandbox mode
- **File naming**: ` *E2ETest.java`

### What NOT to Test in E2E
- Edge cases (those belong in unit tests)
- Error handling details (unit tests)
- All validation combinations (unit tests)